From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:44:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/26] plan9: std's test suite in the guest

std's unit tests link a second std: the assembly as naked functions (each copy its own),
the C exports (malloc, __plan9_*) only outside cfg(test), PRIVTOP and MAIN_PID one instance
(sgx's export_name + available_externally); current() takes ThreadData only of its own pid
(a proc's slots are its parent's copy).

Fixes: Instant signed (timespec's range); OpenOptions checked as unix; set_times sets the
mtime, the atime left (stat(5)); remove_dir_all as rm -r (the directory read whole first);
ExitStatus::code as APE's wait; a NUL in the program name InvalidInput; dial and announce
of numeric addresses through /net/<proto>/clone, not /net/cs (it stopped answering under
load); "malformed address", "bad ip address" InvalidInput; read_buf of sockets uninitialized.

Tests: what Plan 9 has not (symbolic and hard links, setting the atime, TCP half close,
reading back keepalive and ttl, linger, nonblocking, peek, Nagle, NUL in env values) ignored
with a reason; the path separator, $path, rwlock's limit, env and the shell for plan9.
remote-test-server builds for plan9. amd64: 343 passed, 2 failed (TCP under load), 39 ignored;
the integration tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
